Third-party material and services used by Price Accordion – Hintahaitari
=========================================================================

Our own code and documents are under the MIT licence (see LICENSE), except as listed here.

Meta Wearables Device Access Toolkit (DAT) and its sample app
  - The SDK is not included in this repository. The Xcode project fetches it as a Swift package
    (https://github.com/facebook/meta-wearables-dat-ios, pinned to 1.0.1). Using it means accepting the Meta
    Wearables Developer Terms: https://wearables.developer.meta.com/terms
  - The iOS app started from Meta's "CameraAccess" sample. The Swift files that still carry the header
    "Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates" (and the sample's test video and image in
    ios-app/PriceSense/TestResources, and the app icon) are Meta's material, kept with their headers, and stay under
    Meta's terms, not under our MIT licence.

Lens art (design/glasses, ios-app/PriceSense/Glasses/HUD)
  - Generated with Retro Diffusion in an 8-bit arcade style, then cleaned by design/glasses/process_assets.py.
    Check the generator's terms before reusing the art outside this project.

S-Pankki challenge data
  - The synthetic dataset from the Junction 2026 S-Pankki challenge is NOT included. docs/spankki_data.md is a summary of
    its structure and aggregate figures. The tables built from it (data/spankki/monthly.csv and customers.csv) are
    git-ignored on purpose. The customers are synthetic, never real people.

Online services (you bring your own keys; see README and .env.example)
  - NVIDIA Build API (Nemotron) and Context.dev (live web data: respect each site's terms). Their terms apply to your use of them.

Python dependencies (server/pyproject.toml, server/uv.lock) and the other Swift packages keep their own licences.
